2. If `roots` is not provided, gets all subjects that appear in triples with the given property
3. Finds all nodes that appear as objects (parents) in the hierarchy
4. Returns the set difference between potential roots and non-roots (nodes that appear as parents)

This implementation follows the assumption that triples are of the form (child, prop, parent) and finds nodes that are not children of any other node in the hierarchy.

